        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 9:30PM PDT until September 26 at 11:00AM PDT by NWS Eureka CA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, north winds 20 to 25 kt with gusts
to 35 kt and seas 9 to 10 feet expected. For the Small Craft
Advisory, north winds 20 to 25 kt with gusts to 30 kt and seas
8 to 10 feet.

* WHERE...Waters from Cape Mendocino to Pt. Arena CA from 10 to
60 nm.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, from 2 AM to 11 AM PDT Saturday.
For the Small Craft Advisory, until 2 AM PDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
